      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "b1c2d3e4-f5a6-4b7c-8d9e-0f1a2b3c4d05",
      "key": "12cf7890-f053-5734-afcc-0abc67945542",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "<p>The National Food Safety Authority was established by Law 1/2017, with its Executive Regulation issued by Prime Ministerial Decree 412/2019. It took over all food control in 2020, bringing the previously separate control bodies under one authority.</p><p>NFSA sets food-safety rules in line with international standards (Codex Alimentarius), registers, licenses and inspects food establishments, controls food imports and exports, registers special foods, handles consumer complaints and issues alerts.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "62cd108b-d89b-513a-b90a-2847279e7631",
